  "notes": [
    "Level Select now uses one shared grid for all four incident folders. Paper files, folder tabs, preview slots, titles and action buttons have matching dimensions and aligned row/column anchors.",
    "The Last Harvest and The Ossuary have full-size sealed folders with redacted locations, inked-out details, lock marks and disabled Coming Soon actions. These files remain planned, and cannot be started from the selector.",
    "Briarwake replaces the farmer concept portrait with an actual native level preview showing its blood moon, stars, lantern and hedge silhouette. Both playable files use the same Level Preview caption and image dimensions.",
    "The native UI review covered 396 draw states across four resolutions and three HUD sizes, with zero measured clipping or overlap findings. Independent screenshot and geometry review confirmed all twelve selector variants, loaded preview textures and both disabled Coming Soon buttons. Native control/settings checks passed.",
    "Includes the previous survivor grip, arm-motion, sleeve and detailed flashlight improvements. No new gameplay, networking or monster changes in this UI pass.",
    "Blackwater and Briarwake support offline solo or private 2-4 player invite-code co-op. Corn Maze and Stone Labyrinth remain planned. Windows keyboard and mouse alpha; no saved run progress.",
    "Close the game, then choose Update & restart in the launcher. Everyone in a lobby should use the same build. The installer includes the full game and launcher."
  ],
